§§ `A. Tier, s 341 and the Order (C001, C005, C006, C008 to C017)`

-- C001: 7,703 for every month of 2026.
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 3 `of` 2026 EQUALS 7_703
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 11 `of` 2026 EQUALS 7_703
-- C008, C009: the amount's reading of the quarter's first month does not matter in 2026 (same figure, any average wage).
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 3 `of` 2026 `, the average wage of the quarter's first month being` 13_566 EQUALS 7_703
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 11 `of` 2026 `, the average wage of the quarter's first month being` 13_566 EQUALS 7_703
-- C002 (tier 2025 = 7,522 per s 334 note; derived 60% x 12,536.67): the encoding's 60% x 12,536 = 7,521.6 is the same figure to the shekel.
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 12 `of` 2025 `, the average wage of the quarter's first month being` 12_536 EQUALS 7_521.6
-- C003, C004: 2027 and 2029 need the published figure.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 1 `of` 2027 BECAUSE "the reduced collection threshold for 2027 or 2028 had not been published when this encoding was made"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 1 `of` 2029 BECAUSE "the reduced collection threshold from 2029 depends on average wages not known when this encoding was made"
-- C010, C011, C012: art 4 (to 31.3.2000 inclusive) and the amended s 1.
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 4 — s 1 reaches an employee, by this section alone, on the day` (YMD 1999 2 15)
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 4 — s 1 reaches an employee, by this section alone, on the day` (YMD 2000 3 31)
#ASSERT NOT `Order of 5759-1999 s 4 — s 1 reaches an employee, by this section alone, on the day` (YMD 2000 4 1)
-- C013 EXPECT-REFUSED (OURS-WRONG, minor; line 129): I decided the Order does NOT apply to the day 31.12.1998 (art 3 starts it on 1.1.1999);
-- the encoding refuses by naming the repealed Order No. 2. The boolean "applies" is FALSE on the text.
#ASSERT NOT `Order of 5759-1999 s 3 — the Order applies to contributions payable for the day` (YMD 1998 12 31)
-- C014 (Order No. 2 repealed from the commencement): the day before commencement is outside.
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 3 — the Order applies to contributions payable for the day` (YMD 1999 1 1)
-- C015, C016: s 341 needs the Minister's order and the Finance Committee's approval.
#ASSERT     `s 341 — the order is validly made` (`An order under section 341` WITH `made by the Minister` IS TRUE, `approved by the Finance Committee of the Knesset` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 341 — the order is validly made` (`An order under section 341` WITH `made by the Minister` IS TRUE, `approved by the Finance Committee of the Knesset` IS FALSE)
-- C007 (flagged AMBIGUITY: half the average wage 6,783 vs 7,703): EXPECT-REFUSED is not what the encoding does; it answers 7,703
-- with a note that nothing turns on it. Asserted here at my primary reading; agrees.
#ASSERT `Order of 5759-1999 s 1 — the amount of wage or income for the month` 6 `of` 2026 `, the average wage of the quarter's first month being` 13_566 EQUALS 7_703

§§ `B. Several employers, regs 2 to 9 (C066 to C093)`

-- C066 (one of them): coordinated premium on 14,000 = 520.9012 (1.04% x 7,703 + 7.00% x 6,297); A's actual deduction 6,000 x 1.04% = 62.40.
-- The secondary employer B deducts the difference: 520.9012 - 62.40 = 458.5012.
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(a) — the sum the secondary employer may be allowed to deduct: coordinated contributions` 520.9012 `, the others having deducted` 62.4 EQUALS 458.5012
-- C067: coordinated on 6,000 total = 62.40; A deducted 31.2; B deducts 31.2.
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(a) — the sum the secondary employer may be allowed to deduct: coordinated contributions` 62.4 `, the others having deducted` 31.2 EQUALS 31.2
-- C068, C069: 1 January certificate covers January to June; 1 July covers July to December.
#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b)-(c) — the secondary employer may deduct for month` 4 `of` 2026 `, the certificate being` `fid: wage certificate 1 January 2026` `, he having begun on` (YMD 2025 6 10) `and worked in the month being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b)-(c) — the secondary employer may deduct for month` 8 `of` 2026 `, the certificate being` `fid: wage certificate 1 January 2026` `, he having begun on` (YMD 2025 6 10) `and worked in the month being` TRUE
#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b)-(c) — the secondary employer may deduct for month` 9 `of` 2026 `, the certificate being` `fid: wage certificate 1 July 2026` `, he having begun on` (YMD 2025 6 10) `and worked in the month being` TRUE
-- C071, C072: a start on 10 February: the certificate is due at the start of February (1 February); on 5 August, 1 August.
#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b)-(c) — the secondary employer may deduct for month` 2 `of` 2026 `, the certificate being` `fid: wage certificate 1 February 2026` `, he having begun on` (YMD 2026 2 10) `and worked in the month being` TRUE
#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 3A(b)-(c) — the secondary employer may deduct for month` 8 `of` 2026 `, the certificate being` `fid: wage certificate 1 August 2026` `, he having begun on` (YMD 2026 8 5) `and worked in the month being` TRUE
-- C060, C061: the full-rate deduction is an input; at 7.00% on 6,000 recognized employer A deducts 420.
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 2 — where` TRUE `, the deduction from a wage of` 6_000 `at the full rate` 0.07 EQUALS 420
-- C062: a recognized employer deducts the full rate also below the tier: same function, wage 3,000.
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 2 — where` TRUE `, the deduction from a wage of` 3_000 `at the full rate` 0.07 EQUALS 210
-- C064: the form.
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 2A — the employee is bound to fill in the Institute's form` TRUE
-- C079, C080: reg 4(a): 51,910 is not above the maximum; 51,911 is.
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 4(a) — the employee must file an account: highest monthly income` 51_910 `, maximum income` 51_910 `, certificate under reg 3 being` TRUE `, deduction under reg 3A being` FALSE
#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 4(a) — the employee must file an account: highest monthly income` 51_911 `, maximum income` 51_910 `, certificate under reg 3 being` TRUE `, deduction under reg 3A being` FALSE
-- C082: income above the maximum but neither a certificate nor a reg 3A deduction: no report.
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 4(a) — the employee must file an account: highest monthly income` 60_000 `, maximum income` 51_910 `, certificate under reg 3 being` FALSE `, deduction under reg 3A being` FALSE
-- C081: report for 2026 due 31.7.2027.
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 4(a) — the day by which the account is due, for the tax year` 2026 EQUALS YMD 2027 7 31
-- C085, C086, C087: 31.12.2033 is the last day for 2026; refund for a month of 2026; one day later the text says nothing.
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 6(a) — the last day to file the account for the tax year` 2026 EQUALS YMD 2033 12 31
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 6(a) — the refund for a month of the tax year` 2026 `, the account filed on` (YMD 2033 12 31) `, deducted` 1_200 `, coordinated contributions` 1_000 EQUALS 200
-- C088: three months after receipt.
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 6(b) — the day by which the refund is due: request received` (YMD 2026 1 31) `, doubt being` FALSE EQUALS YMD 2026 4 30
-- C089: the s 353 due day of an employee: the 15th of the month after the payment period.
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 7(1) — the day the excess is taken to have been paid, before any move under s 353(b), for month` 3 `of` 2026 EQUALS YMD 2026 4 15
-- C090, C091: reg 8, reg 9.
#ASSERT NOT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 8 — regulations 2 and 3 apply to a monthly income paid for the day` (YMD 1997 2 28)
#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 8 — regulations 2 and 3 apply to a monthly income paid for the day` (YMD 1997 3 1)
#ASSERT `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 9 — the equal part deducted in each of the five months` 1_000 EQUALS 200
-- C063: whether an employer is "recognized" turns on the 1972 Order: an input.
#ASSERT     `Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 2 — the regulation reaches an employer:` TRUE `, or one to whom` FALSE

§§ `C. s 340, 340A, 343, 336 (C099 to C141)`

-- C101, C102: maternity premium for an Area resident who is not an Israeli resident: 70% of item 1. Item 1 above the tier 1.40 for an employee.
#ASSERT `s 340(c) — the maternity insurance rate: item 1 rate` 1.40 `, a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli resident there being` TRUE EQUALS 0.98
#ASSERT `s 340(c) — the maternity insurance rate: item 1 rate` 0.24 `, a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli resident there being` TRUE EQUALS 0.168
-- C103: 0.53% x 6,783 = 35.9499. C104: 2027 with no order: 0.4% x 6,783 = 27.132.
#ASSERT `s 340(d) — the monthly work-injury contribution for training or rehabilitation, year` 2026 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE `, the average wage being` 13_566 EQUALS 35.9499
#ASSERT `s 340(d) — the monthly work-injury contribution for training or rehabilitation, year` 2027 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE `, the average wage being` 13_566 EQUALS 27.132
-- C106: 0.13% x 6,783 = 8.8179.
#ASSERT `s 340(e) — the monthly maternity contribution for vocational training, year` 2026 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE `, the average wage being` 13_566 EQUALS 8.8179
-- C111, C112: both temporary figures for 2025 as for 2026.
#ASSERT `s 340(d) — the monthly work-injury contribution for training or rehabilitation, year` 2025 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE `, the average wage being` 13_566 EQUALS 35.9499
#ASSERT `s 340(e) — the monthly maternity contribution for vocational training, year` 2025 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE `, the average wage being` 13_566 EQUALS 8.8179
-- C113 to C116: 7.85% of the quarter's wage, 2026.
#ASSERT `s 340A — the employer's contributions for a household worker for a quarter, year` 2026 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE `, wage` 0 `, insured under Chapter 11 and not under section 351(b) or (d) being` TRUE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 340A — the employer's contributions for a household worker for a quarter, year` 2026 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE `, wage` 1_000 `, insured under Chapter 11 and not under section 351(b) or (d) being` TRUE EQUALS 78.5
#ASSERT `s 340A — the employer's contributions for a household worker for a quarter, year` 2026 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE `, wage` 6_000 `, insured under Chapter 11 and not under section 351(b) or (d) being` TRUE EQUALS 471
#ASSERT `s 340A — the employer's contributions for a household worker for a quarter, year` 2026 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE `, wage` 12_000 `, insured under Chapter 11 and not under section 351(b) or (d) being` TRUE EQUALS 942
-- C117: deduction 1.8% of 6,000 = 108. C118: uninsured 3.6% of 6,000 = 216. C119, C120: s 351(b) or (d) applies: also 3.6%.
#ASSERT `s 340A(a)(2) — the most the employer may deduct from the worker's wage for a quarter, year` 2026 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE `, wage` 6_000 EQUALS 108
#ASSERT `s 340A — the employer's contributions for a household worker for a quarter, year` 2026 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE `, wage` 6_000 `, insured under Chapter 11 and not under section 351(b) or (d) being` FALSE EQUALS 216
-- C124, C125, C126: before 2025 no s 340A; January 2025 and 2027 (no order) use the base figures 6.25%.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 340A — the employer's contributions for a household worker for a quarter, year` 2024 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE `, wage` 3_000 `, insured under Chapter 11 and not under section 351(b) or (d) being` TRUE BECAUSE "this provision was added by Amendment No. 252 from 1 January 2025 and did not exist before"
#ASSERT `s 340A — the employer's contributions for a household worker for a quarter, year` 2025 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE `, wage` 3_000 `, insured under Chapter 11 and not under section 351(b) or (d) being` TRUE EQUALS 235.5
#ASSERT `s 340A — the employer's contributions for a household worker for a quarter, year` 2027 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE `, wage` 3_000 `, insured under Chapter 11 and not under section 351(b) or (d) being` TRUE EQUALS 187.5
-- C130 to C133: s 343.
#ASSERT     `s 343 — the employer is one the Minister may approve` (`An employer's position under section 343` WITH `the number of employees` IS 500, `bound by law, a collective agreement or a contract to pay wages for the time injury allowance is paid` IS TRUE, `the total wages the employer pays for that time` IS 10_000, `the injury allowance paid for that time` IS 10_000)
#ASSERT NOT `s 343 — the employer is one the Minister may approve` (`An employer's position under section 343` WITH `the number of employees` IS 499, `bound by law, a collective agreement or a contract to pay wages for the time injury allowance is paid` IS TRUE, `the total wages the employer pays for that time` IS 10_000, `the injury allowance paid for that time` IS 10_000)
#ASSERT NOT `s 343 — the employer is one the Minister may approve` (`An employer's position under section 343` WITH `the number of employees` IS 500, `bound by law, a collective agreement or a contract to pay wages for the time injury allowance is paid` IS TRUE, `the total wages the employer pays for that time` IS 9_000, `the injury allowance paid for that time` IS 10_000)
#ASSERT NOT `s 343 — the employer is one the Minister may approve` (`An employer's position under section 343` WITH `the number of employees` IS 500, `bound by law, a collective agreement or a contract to pay wages for the time injury allowance is paid` IS FALSE, `the total wages the employer pays for that time` IS 10_000, `the injury allowance paid for that time` IS 10_000)
-- C134: the reduced amount is the Minister's.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 343 — the reduced contribution for an approved employer` (`An employer's position under section 343` WITH `the number of employees` IS 600, `bound by law, a collective agreement or a contract to pay wages for the time injury allowance is paid` IS TRUE, `the total wages the employer pays for that time` IS 12_000, `the injury allowance paid for that time` IS 10_000) BECAUSE "the reduced contributions the Minister determined under section 343 are not in the sources"
-- C139, C140: s 336.
#ASSERT `s 336 — the last day of the payment period holding the day` (YMD 2026 3 17) `, other limits having been set being` FALSE EQUALS YMD 2026 3 31
#ASSERT `s 336 — the last day of the payment period holding the day` (YMD 2028 2 10) `, other limits having been set being` FALSE EQUALS YMD 2028 2 29

§§ `D. s 28, 28A, 28B, 32 (C143 to C186)`

-- C143 to C147 EXPECT-FAIL (TESTER-WRONG; lines 220 to 223 and 225): I divided by the printed total 14.60; the printed cells for an employee above the tier
-- add to 14.49, so the ratio is cell / 14.49. 1,000 x 1.40 / 14.60 = 95.8904; the encoding gives 1,000 x 1.40 / 14.49 = 96.6184.
#ASSERT `s 28(a) — the sum credited to the account of the branch` `maternity` `from a payment of` 1_000 `, the rates being` `fid: employee rates above the tier, as printed cells (2024 to 2027 work-injury 2.06)` EQUALS (1_000 TIMES 1.40 DIVIDED BY 14.60)
#ASSERT `s 28(a) — the sum credited to the account of the branch` `children` `from a payment of` 1_000 `, the rates being` `fid: employee rates above the tier, as printed cells (2024 to 2027 work-injury 2.06)` EQUALS (1_000 TIMES 2.08 DIVIDED BY 14.60)
#ASSERT `s 28(a) — the sum credited to the account of the branch` `work injury` `from a payment of` 1_000 `, the rates being` `fid: employee rates above the tier, as printed cells (2024 to 2027 work-injury 2.06)` EQUALS (1_000 TIMES 2.06 DIVIDED BY 14.60)
#ASSERT `s 28(a) — the sum credited to the account of the branch` `senior citizens and survivors` `from a payment of` 1_000 `, the rates being` `fid: employee rates above the tier, as printed cells (2024 to 2027 work-injury 2.06)` EQUALS (1_000 TIMES 5.89 DIVIDED BY 14.60)
-- C147: half paid, half credited (the same ratio, proportional amounts), at the cell total 14.49: maternity 500 x 1.40 / 14.49.
