§§ `E. s 2 and Schedule A (C188 to C194, C363 to C370)`

-- C188: December, November measured 13,700, no compensation: 13,700 x 1.005 = 13,768.5.
#ASSERT `s 2(a) — the corrected measured wage: the month before measured` 13_700 `, that month being exceptional:` FALSE `, the month before it measured` 11_000 `, compensation then` `fid: no compensation` `and in the earlier exceptional month` `fid: no compensation` EQUALS 13_768.5
-- C190: November itself exceptional, October measured 13,600: 13,600 x 1.005 = 13,668.
#ASSERT `s 2(a) — the corrected measured wage: the month before measured` 13_700 `, that month being exceptional:` TRUE `, the month before it measured` 13_600 `, compensation then` `fid: no compensation` `and in the earlier exceptional month` `fid: no compensation` EQUALS 13_668
-- C192: (13,200 - 12,000) / 12,000 = 0.1 (the 14,200 / 13,768.5 case has no short decimal).
#ASSERT `s 2(b)(2) — the monthly difference: measured` 13_200 `and corrected` 12_000 EQUALS 0.1
-- C193: differences 0.03, 0.02, 0.04: sum 0.09, a twelfth 0.0075: 13,000 x 1.0075 = 13,097.5.
#ASSERT `s 2(b)(2) — the average wage increased: computed` 13_000 `with the monthly differences` (LIST 0.03, 0.02, 0.04) EQUALS 13_097.5
-- C187: December is exceptional; so is a month in which clothing or recuperation allowances were paid.
#ASSERT     `s 2(a) — month` 12 `is an exceptional wage month, allowances to most employees being` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 2(a) — month` 3 `is an exceptional wage month, allowances to most employees being` FALSE
#ASSERT     `s 2(a) — month` 3 `is an exceptional wage month, allowances to most employees being` TRUE
-- C363: 15% x 13,566 = 2,034.90 for every month of a quarter. C195 (the two 2026 figures): with 13,769 it would be 2,065.35.
#ASSERT `Schedule A — the minimum average monthly income for month` 2 `, the average wage on the first day of the quarter's first month being` 13_566 EQUALS 2_034.9
#ASSERT `Schedule A — the minimum average monthly income for month` 12 `, the average wage on the first day of the quarter's first month being` 13_566 EQUALS 2_034.9
#ASSERT `Schedule A — the minimum average monthly income for month` 5 `, the average wage on the first day of the quarter's first month being` 13_769 EQUALS 2_065.35

